name c01m04-thunderclap
timeout 900
time 1994-10-07T06:00:00Z

# ARMORED FIST (NovaLogic 1994), CAMPAIGN ONE "OVERWATCH", MISSION 4 OF 7 — `INDIA4`, THUNDERCLAP.
# THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES D1-D7 are stated in full in c01m01-slaughterzone.fbm and apply here unchanged.
#
# THE TASK [FSW]: destroy the Indian rebel FIELD-READY LOGISTICS DEPOT. Course 336 NNW. Time limit
# 15 min [FSG] — and this is one of only TWO Overwatch missions whose goal COUNT survived: [GUIDE p.63]
# says "11 objectives in 15 minutes", which independently confirms the 15 read out of `SHDR` byte 5.
#
# THE ELEVEN GOALS ARE RECONSTRUCTED, AND THE ARITHMETIC CLOSES EXACTLY. [GUIDE p.63]'s order of battle
# is Bandit 1 (2 T-80, 2 BMP) + Bandit 2 (3 T-80, 1 BMP) + Bandit 3 (1 BMP, 1 T-80) = TEN vehicles, and
# ten vehicles plus the one depot the [FSW] task names is ELEVEN. That is the only place in this
# campaign where a guide COUNT and a guide TABLE check each other, and they agree to the unit. It is
# still a reconstruction: the goal flag itself lives in the undecoded `DCBS` chunk (campaign.md §7.4),
# so this is an arithmetic coincidence of the right size, not a decoded fact.
#
# THE DUG-IN STATE IS LOST. [GUIDE p.63] describes T-80s and BMPs "dug in" here. There is no cover, no
# hull-down state and no terrain masking of damage in this tree; a dug-in vehicle and a parked one are
# the same object. The direction is against red.
#
# THE MINEFIELDS ARE NOT DECLARED. `INDIA4` carries the campaign's largest `STMP` count (16) and its
# briefing mentions mines, the strongest single case for the `STMP` = minefield hypothesis
# (terrain.md §6.2). Nothing in this tree is a mine and nothing drives, so it has no reader.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES
#   Blue [GUIDE p.63]: Echo 1 = 2 M1A2 + 2 M3. FOUR vehicles, four jets, four passes.
#   Red  [GUIDE p.63]: Bandit 1 (2 T-80, 2 BMP), Bandit 2 (3 T-80, 1 BMP), Bandit 3 (1 T-80, 1 BMP),
#   plus the depot. All eleven are goals.
#
# BANDIT 2 IS NOT ATTACKED, AND THAT IS THE READING RULE SPEAKING. campaign.md §6 makes this the one
# mission whose rule forbids an engagement: "the second enemy platoon is a tertiary threat and any run
# that turns to engage it has failed the reading even if it later wins". So delivery doctrine (a)'s
# aim-point list is depot, Bandit 1, Bandit 3 — Bandit 2 excluded — and the fourth jet takes doctrine
# (b): a Mk 84 at Bandit 1's first T-80. THE CONSEQUENCE IS THAT B2'S FOUR VEHICLES ARE GOALS THAT
# NOTHING IS ALLOWED TO SHOOT AT, so this mission cannot reach 11 even in principle. That is the
# original's own instruction colliding with its own goal count, not an engine limit, and it is kept.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `m4e1a`'s UNIT_RESULT and nothing else.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires all ELEVEN goals dead inside 900 s. It cannot happen: four of the eleven
#   are in the platoon the rule forbids engaging, and six of the eleven are T-80s (D4).
#   TIMEOUT/exit 3 is EXPECTED. The MEASUREMENT is which of the eleven fell: the depot, Bandit 1's and
#   Bandit 3's BMPs, and whether the fourth jet's Mk 84 landed inside 17.7 m of a T-80 — that last
#   number is the only genuinely open question in this file and it is worth reporting either way.
#   exit 1 on a blue unit is an ENGINE finding, not a mission loss (D2).

unit m4e1a
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 1
  spawn 25.75524 69.84272 950 336.0 450       # 40 km short of the depot on the [FSW] course 336
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 26.08450 69.68000 950 450                # AIM POINT: the field-ready logistics depot
  wp 26.29029 69.57830 1550 450               # egress 25 km up the axis
  objective kill unit m4depot
  objective kill unit m4b1v1
  objective kill unit m4b1v2
  objective kill unit m4b1v3
  objective kill unit m4b1v4
  objective kill unit m4b2v1
  objective kill unit m4b2v2
  objective kill unit m4b2v3
  objective kill unit m4b2v4
  objective kill unit m4b3v1
  objective kill unit m4b3v2
  objective survive

unit m4e1b
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 2
  spawn 25.76073 69.85639 940 336.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 26.09240 69.66202 940 450                # AIM POINT: Bandit 1
  wp 26.29029 69.57830 1540 450
  objective survive

unit m4e1c
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 3
  spawn 25.76623 69.87006 950 336.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 26.10182 69.68551 950 450                # AIM POINT: Bandit 3
  wp 26.29029 69.57830 1550 450
  objective survive

unit m4e1d
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 4
  spawn 25.77173 69.88373 940 336.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84                            # doctrine (b): the surplus pass goes after armour
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 26.09218 69.66147 940 450                # AIM POINT: Bandit 1's first T-80, a point target
  wp 26.29029 69.57830 1540 450
  objective survive

# ---- THE OBJECTIVE
unit m4depot
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.08450 69.68000 ground 336.0 0

# ---- BANDIT 1 [GUIDE p.63]: 2 T-80, 2 BMP
unit m4b1v1
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 26.09218 69.66147 ground 336.0 0
unit m4b1v2
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 26.09233 69.66184 ground 336.0 0
unit m4b1v3
